{
  "name": "Cold - [MMMM]",
  "img": "icons/magic/water/snowflake-ice-snow-white.webp",
  "description": "Simply put, the cold makes you slow and stupid. Expect your patients to be numb, clumsy, and frostbitten. Fortunately, there is an easy solution to almost every wintery woe: warm them back up. You will need a crackling fire, thick blankets, or at the very least, the body heat of a willing volunteer. Do not rewarm them too fast, mind you. Slow and gentle, like thawing meat from the icebox.",
